Design a 4-to-2 priority encoder that produces a 2-bit output based on the highest priority input from a 4-bit input vector. The encoder assesses the input signals using combinational logic, with the outputs reflecting the index of the highest-order active input. The results are then registered on the positive edge of a clock signal to provide a synchronous output. The module effectively translates active inputs into a binary representation of their priority while ensuring data stability with the clocking mechanism.
