Implement a binary-coded decimal (BCD) to seven-segment display decoder. The module takes a 4-bit BCD input, representing values from 0 to 9, and outputs an 8-bit signal that encodes the corresponding seven-segment display representation. When the input corresponds to a valid BCD digit, the output activates the appropriate segments of the display; for inputs outside the valid range, the output will be set to display nothing (all segments OFF).
module top_module(
	in , out
    );

code:
module top_module(
	in , out
    );input [3:0] in;
output reg [7:0] out;

always @(in) begin

		case (in)
			0: out = 8'b11111100;
			1: out = 8'b01100000;
			2: out = 8'b11011010;
			3: out = 8'b11110010;
			4: out = 8'b01100110;
			5: out = 8'b10110110;
			6: out = 8'b10111110;
			7: out = 8'b11100000;
			8: out = 8'b11111110;
			9: out = 8'b11110110;

			default : out = 00000000;
		endcase
end		

endmodule

