Design a circuit that converts a 22-bit floating-point representation into an 8-bit integer output. The input consists of a sign bit, a 5-bit exponent, and a 16-bit fraction, from which the output is derived based on the value of the exponent. The conversion function evaluates the exponent to determine how to truncate or pad the fraction, producing different 8-bit integer values depending on the exponent's range, with special cases for maximum and default conditions.
